    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d507-a3">

                <pb facs="0672" n="552" sameAs="frus:frus1905/pg552"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 3.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Minister Powell to the Minister of Foreign
                        Relations.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Port au
                                Prince</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1905-06-13"><hi rendition="#italic">June 13,
                        1905</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge receipt of
                    your excellency’s favor of to-day’s date, in which you request information as to
                    the reason which led Mr. Charles Cameau to seek asylum at our legation.</p>
                <p>In reply to your excellency’s request, I am unable to forward to you the
                    information asked. On coming to our legation he informed me that his personal
                    liberty was in danger and requested asylum from us.</p>
                <p>Since Mr. Cameau has been here several persons connected with your excellency’s
                    government have had interviews with him. Among this number were: The President’s
                    private secretary, Mr. Gabrielle; your excellency’s colleague, Hon. F. Marcelin,
                    and the president of the chamber of deputies. Possibly one of the above can give
                    you the required information that you request of me.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">W. F. Powell.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
